                <pb facs="0569" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v24/pg545"/>

                <head>248. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Laos<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d248-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-12-27T19:41:00-05:00">December 27, 1961,
                            7:41 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>571. Eyes Only from Secretary.</p>
                <p>Assume you will be seeing Souvanna at first appropriate opportunity in order to
                    move forward negotiations with or without direct participation RLG, and that you
                    will also be concerting your efforts with British and French.</p>
                <p>This telegram confirms that you have full authority to take action necessary to
                    bring about formation of coalition government we can accept. This means that if
                    you find Souvanna is prepared to negotiate for a reasonable composition of
                    government and if Boun Oum and Phoumi continue their obstructive tactics, you
                    are free to take such action as you may consider necessary to achieve our
                    objectives, even to the point of informing Boun Oum and Phoumi that we will no
                    longer support them and so inform the King, urging him to call for their
                    resignation and appoint a new Prime Minister prepared to carry on negotiations
                    in good faith.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d248-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d248-f1-content">
